---
title: Fluffy Japanese Pancakes
yield: 8%pancakes
course: Breakfast
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

In a large bowl mix the @plain flour{200%g}, @icing sugar{3%tbsp}, @baking powder{2%tsp}, and @salt{pinch}.

In a jug whisk together the @milk{600%ml}, @unsalted butter{4%tbsp}(melted), @vanilla extract{0.5%tsp}, and @egg yolk{1}. Stir into the flour mixture.

In another large bowl beat the @egg whites{3} with the @cream of tartar{0.25%tsp} until stiff peaks form. Fold one-third of the beaten egg whites into the flour mixture. Gently fold in the remaining egg whites until just combined (do not overmix).

Lightly spray a #frying pan{} and the inside of #four ring moulds{} with oil. Place on a medium-low heat.

Half fill each ring mold with batter. Cover with a lid and cook for ~{5%minutes} until the batter rises to the top of the moulds and the bottom is golden.

Use a spatula to lift the pancakes onto the lid, cover with the upturned frying pan, and flip over. Cook for a further ~{5%minutes}.

> Serve with butter and maple syrup. Eat before the pancakes deflate.

Re-spray the frying pan and moulds, and repeat the cooking method with the remaining batter.